From 303d97b067bc05ad94bafcd315075e6e52716fb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 19:28:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02418/11362] [outer-loop] register a GameAdapter for tu93
 (frame-based; L1 verifier-routed, reproducible)

Registered the second GameAdapter (after lp85's reference adapter). tu93 is a
4-direction keyboard maze; FRAME-BASED RE (no internal-state read), the player =
the moving colour-9 sprite, the goal = the static colour-14 marker (RE'd by
motion). The hand_verifier is the player->goal Manhattan distance, turning the
OfflineSolver's BFS into goal-distance-routed best-first search; state_key is the
full-grid dedup.

VALIDATED: solve_adaptered('tu93', 1) -> reached L1 in 18 moves,
offline_reproduced=True (the goal-distance verifier routes the L1 solve).

KNOWN LIMITATION at L2+ (documented in the adapter + this commit, NOT a false
claim): tu93 carries HIDDEN/RNG state beyond the rendered grid that the
OfflineSolver's REUSED single env accumulates across the search, so a
verifier-found L2 path does NOT reproduce on a fresh env -- the reproduction gate
correctly rejects it (offline_reproduced=False). graph_explore avoids this by
DEEPCOPYING the env per node; the OfflineSolver does not. Deep-solving tu93 via
this adapter therefore needs a deepcopy-per-node (fresh-env) mode in
arc_solver_kit.OfflineSolver -- a kit-level change, not an adapter fix.

3 unit tests (registration + frame-based verifier/state_key on synthetic grids);
ruff + spec-coverage clean. Did not modify the shared OfflineSolver or registry
(conductor is active on ARC).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
